# `invert` reads and stores p[i]: the front end expects a list of numbers of p, lists do arrive, and the function has a guard that tests for one. This caller hands it a view of clamped bytes that it has made itself: the argument cannot pass
# the guard. The callee was not copied for that reason: the call went to the guard, which fails every time, and on to the slow body. It is copied: no test is laid for p, the body is walked with the view. f2 = run.
# RUN: walk f2 mechanisms=all
# CHECK: isLoopHead=true
# CHECK: = GetTypedArrayElement
# CHECK: = PutTypedArrayElement
# CHECK-NOT: role=ParameterGuard
# -- source: a-callee-whose-guard-the-argument-cannot-pass-is-copied-with-the-arguments-own-type.cjs
